WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.074 --> 00:00:01.080
(upbeat music)

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:02.520
- [Narrator] These
bubbles in the Baltic Sea

00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:05.850
flared up after explosions on
the Nord Stream gas pipeline

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:08.310
since September, 2022.

00:00:08.310 --> 00:00:11.910
The incident prompted several
international investigations.

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:15.390
Western officials initially
accused Russia of sabotage

00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:17.700
while Moscow denied this.

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:21.270
Now more details of the
probes are starting to emerge.

00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:23.370
- The German prosecutor announced

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:25.950
that they had searched a rental yacht

00:00:25.950 --> 00:00:30.810
that was possibly linked to
the attack on the pipelines.

00:00:30.810 --> 00:00:33.210
- [Narrator] They also
said a pro-Ukrainian group

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:35.010
may have been responsible,

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:38.580
but Ukrainian officials
denied any involvement.

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:41.250
So here's what we know so
far about the explosions

00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:44.403
that hit some of Europe's
most important pipelines.

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:50.280
The Nord Stream and
Nord Stream 2 pipelines

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:53.283
were built to transfer
gas from Russia to Europe.

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:55.920
A Russian gas giant, Gazprom,

00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:59.490
stopped deliveries through
Nord Stream in August, 2022

00:00:59.490 --> 00:01:01.563
saying the pipes needed repairs.

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:06.000
Nord Stream 2 was built, but
wasn't up and running yet

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:08.400
because Germany stopped its certification

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:11.370
just before Russia's invasion of Ukraine.

00:01:11.370 --> 00:01:13.590
Then in September, 2022,

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:16.143
the pipelines were damaged in explosions.

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:19.050
Germany, Sweden, and Denmark,

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:21.600
the three countries
closest to the incident,

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:25.170
launched separate
investigations into the cause.

00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:27.750
Early findings said the
blasts were deliberate

00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:30.510
and caused leaks in four places,

00:01:30.510 --> 00:01:32.820
and the investigations
looked at the possibility

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:35.160
of Russia as the instigator.

00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:38.223
Moscow has repeatedly
denied any involvement.

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:40.770
In early March,

00:01:40.770 --> 00:01:43.860
German prosecutors said
that two months earlier

00:01:43.860 --> 00:01:45.750
investigators searched a yacht

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:49.050
and found traces of explosives on board.

00:01:49.050 --> 00:01:52.290
- We managed to locate it
in the north of Germany.

00:01:52.290 --> 00:01:56.700
It's a very beautiful,
white, sleek leisure boat

00:01:56.700 --> 00:02:01.700
that has five cabins and can
comfortably sleep 11 people.

00:02:02.790 --> 00:02:05.160
- [Narrator] Investigators
believe the vessel set sail

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:08.103
from a port in northern
Germany on September 6th.

00:02:09.330 --> 00:02:13.080
- Around September the 7th,
it made a pit stop in Wiek

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:16.530
on the island of Rugen,
also in northern Germany.

00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:20.550
There, I think, part of
the crew came on board

00:02:20.550 --> 00:02:25.200
and they loaded the boat with
food and other provisions.

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:28.290
And then from then there's a bit of a gap.

00:02:28.290 --> 00:02:31.830
And then the boat reemerges
on the 16th of September

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:34.650
on the Danish island of Christianso,

00:02:34.650 --> 00:02:36.720
which is close to the area

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:41.160
where the Nord Stream
pipelines were attacked.

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:43.110
- [Narrator] German officials
said a group of people

00:02:43.110 --> 00:02:44.520
rented the boat.

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:46.980
Some of them presented Ukrainian passports

00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:48.990
that may have been forged.

00:02:48.990 --> 00:02:51.823
(speaking German)

00:02:57.570 --> 00:02:58.950
- [Bojan] What we don't know, however,

00:02:58.950 --> 00:03:01.080
is who these people were,

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:03.420
what is exactly their
relationship to Ukraine,

00:03:03.420 --> 00:03:04.890
if they were Ukrainians,

00:03:04.890 --> 00:03:07.560
and whether or not they
have any relationship

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:12.000
to the Ukrainian government or
any kind of formal authority.

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:15.240
- [Narrator] Ukrainian officials
denied any involvement.

00:03:15.240 --> 00:03:18.060
- That's totally against our own interest.

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:19.590
- Russia's president had accused

00:03:19.590 --> 00:03:21.990
what he called Anglo-Saxon powers

00:03:21.990 --> 00:03:24.270
of blowing up the pipelines,

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:26.070
and the Kremlin said Western nations

00:03:26.070 --> 00:03:29.520
rejected its request to
join their investigations.

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:31.800
- One thing that we know for a fact

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:34.350
that these investigators
do not believe anymore

00:03:34.350 --> 00:03:35.973
that Russia was behind it.

00:03:38.430 --> 00:03:40.560
- [Narrator] German
investigators are also looking at

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:43.440
whether the boat was
part of a larger mission

00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:45.360
or a false flag operation

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:48.720
designed to divert attention
from the real culprits.

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:51.990
- We'll see where this leads,
but at the present time,

00:03:51.990 --> 00:03:54.360
it doesn't seem we have more clarity.

00:03:54.360 --> 00:03:59.190
It seems we have even more
layers of obscurity and mystery

00:03:59.190 --> 00:04:02.820
adding to this kind of huge puzzle.

00:04:02.820 --> 00:04:05.370
- [Narrator] The leaks highlighted
concerns about the safety

00:04:05.370 --> 00:04:08.130
of critical energy
infrastructure in Europe.

00:04:08.130 --> 00:04:11.070
- It demonstrates the importance

00:04:11.070 --> 00:04:14.820
of protecting our critical
undersea infrastructure.

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:16.260
- [Narrator] As for the damaged pipes,

00:04:16.260 --> 00:04:19.563
there's no indication that
they'll be repaired anytime soon.

